       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as no more than 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. The order is about twice the daily maximum.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended. If it is, I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the above-maximum dose."
